5.1 AGENT ORCHESTRATOR
- Implement an AgentOrchestrator as a Swift actor that manages a pool of
  specialized sub-agents.
- Agents communicate via a structured message bus (AgentMessage protocol
  with Codable conformance).
- Each agent has: a unique ID, a role enum, a state machine (idle/thinking/
  acting/waiting/error), a memory store, and a tool registry.
- The orchestrator assigns tasks to agents, monitors their state, handles
  failures, and routes results to the appropriate downstream consumer.
- Agent autonomy is gated by the user's autonomy level setting:
  * Manual: agents analyze only, never execute. All actions require approval.
  * Semi-Auto: agents execute low-risk pre-approved action types automatically;
    flag high-risk actions for human approval via push notification + in-app
    modal with countdown timer.
  * Full-Auto: agents execute all approved action types autonomously with
    full audit logging.

5.2 SPECIALIZED AGENTS (implement each as a separate actor):

  MarketAnalystAgent:
  - Receives real-time OHLCV data, order book data, and news feeds.
  - Runs multi-timeframe technical analysis on all watched symbols.
  - Computes and evaluates: RSI, MACD, Bollinger Bands, ATR, Stochastic,
    EMA/SMA crossovers, Fibonacci retracements, support/resistance zones,
    volume profile, VWAP, pivot points.
  - Emits structured AnalysisResult objects with confidence scores.

  FundamentalAnalystAgent:
  - Consumes economic calendar events, COT data, institutional flows,
    news sentiment scores, central bank statements.
  - Builds a fundamental bias score per currency (bullish/bearish/neutral)
    updated in real-time as data arrives.
  - Tracks interest rate differentials and carry trade attractiveness.

  NewsAnalystAgent:
  - Processes each incoming news item through on-device NLP sentiment.
  - Classifies impact: high/medium/low.
  - Identifies which instruments are affected.
  - Aggregates news sentiment over configurable rolling windows (1h, 4h, 24h).
  - Emits sentiment shift alerts when aggregated score crosses thresholds.

  SignalGeneratorAgent:
  - Receives outputs from MarketAnalystAgent and FundamentalAnalystAgent.
  - Applies a configurable multi-factor signal fusion algorithm.
  - Supports multiple signal strategies: trend following, mean reversion,
    breakout, news momentum, carry trade, correlation arbitrage.
  - Each signal includes: direction (long/short), entry price, stop loss,
    take profit levels (TP1/TP2/TP3), R:R ratio, confidence score, expiry,
    and reasoning chain (human-readable explanation of why the signal was
    generated, referencing specific indicator values and events).

  RiskManagerAgent:
  - Validates every signal before it reaches execution.
  - Enforces: max risk per trade (configurable %), max daily drawdown limit,
    max open position count, max correlated exposure per currency,
    max position size based on account equity, news event blackout windows.
  - Automatically reduces position size if account equity has dropped.
  - Emits RiskViolation events for any rejected signal with full reason.

  ExecutionAgent:
  - Receives approved signals from RiskManagerAgent.
  - Connects to broker execution APIs (see Phase 7) and places orders.
  - Monitors order fill status. Handles partial fills, rejections, slippage.
  - Reports back actual fill price and slippage to Journal.
  - Implements smart order routing: tries primary broker first, falls back
    to secondary if rejected or timed out.

  PortfolioMonitorAgent:
  - Polls open positions every configurable interval (default: 30 seconds).
  - Detects positions approaching stop loss or take profit.
  - Manages trailing stop logic: adjusts stop loss as position moves in favor.
  - Detects correlation spikes between open positions and alerts user.
  - Closes hedged positions automatically when configured.

  BacktestAgent:
  - Receives a strategy configuration and date range.
  - Runs full historical simulation on locally stored OHLCV data.
  - Reports: total return, Sharpe ratio, Sortino ratio, max drawdown,
    win rate, average R:R, profit factor, monthly breakdown, equity curve.
  - Exports results as an Artifact (see Phase 6).

  CopyTradingAgent:
  - Scrapes ForexFactory Leaderboard and Myfxbook Trade Explorer.
  - Identifies top-performing traders by criteria: win rate, drawdown,
    Sharpe ratio, trade frequency, pair specialization.
  - Optionally mirrors their trades (with configurable position scaling).
  - Tracks copy performance separately from manual trades.

  ResearchAgent:
  - Receives a free-text research query from the user (e.g. "analyze EUR/USD
    outlook for next week").
  - Gathers relevant data: recent OHLCV, news sentiment, economic calendar,
    COT data, analyst picks.
  - Composes a structured research report using LLM (see Phase 5.3).
  - Returns the report as a formatted Artifact (PDF + JSON).

  AnomalyDetectionAgent:
  - Monitors all price feeds for statistical anomalies: flash crashes,
    abnormal spreads, sudden volume spikes.
  - Triggers alerts and optionally halts all automated strategies when
    anomalies are detected.
  - Uses Z-score and IQR methods to classify outliers.

  SchedulerAgent:
  - Manages all time-based tasks across the system.
  - Triggers scraping jobs, analysis runs, report generation, and sync tasks
    on configurable cron-style schedules.
  - Supports one-time, repeating, and market-session-aware scheduling.

