=============================================================================
GLOBAL RULES FOR CODEX THROUGHOUT ALL PHASES:
=============================================================================

- AUDIT FIRST. Scan existing code before writing anything new.
- SKIP IF EXISTS AND WORKING. Fix if exists and broken.
- NO PLACEHOLDERS. No TODOs. No fatalError("not implemented").
- ALL CODE MUST COMPILE. Run a build after every logical commit.
- ALL TESTS MUST PASS before advancing to the next phase.
- COMMIT AFTER EACH MODULE with a descriptive conventional commit message.
- USE ACTORS for all shared mutable state. Swift strict concurrency mode.
- USE COMBINE for all reactive data flows between modules.
- USE ASYNC/AWAIT everywhere. No completion handlers.
- DEPENDENCY INJECTION throughout. No singletons except global actors.
- LOG EVERY ERROR using OSLog with appropriate log level.
- NEVER expose secrets in source code. All keys via Keychain or Secret Manager.
- PAPER TRADING must be the default. Never touch live funds without explicit
  user confirmation and correct autonomy level settings.
- EVERY AGENT ACTION must be logged with full context to the audit log.
- ALL UI UPDATES must occur on the Main actor.
- ALL NETWORKING must support cancellation via Task cancellation.
- HANDLE ALL ERROR CASES. Never use try! or as! in production code paths.
- CLEAN UP RESOURCES. All WebSocket connections, Realm instances, and
  WKWebView instances must be properly torn down.

